  "narrative": "Compared to last sale: In the Southern Central region, feeder steers and steer calves 15.00-20.00 lower. Feeder heifers and heifer calves 15.00-25.00 lower on limited current FOB trades. Demand moderate for steers and light for heifers. CME futures have experienced a sharp decline over the past week and a half, placing additional downward pressure on the cattle market. Supply included: 68 percent from the South Central region, 14 percent from the South East region, 3 percent from the Northeast/Upper Midwest, 6 percent from the North Central region, and 9 percent from the West region. Deliveries are current through February 2027. Current delivery is 14 days from the last day of the video and is up to and including November 19, 2026. Some Beef and Beef on Dairy cattle sold with an .90-1.20 right slide. Supply included: 96% Feeder Cattle (54% Steers, 1% Dairy Steers, 27% Heifers, 11% Beef/Dairy Steers, 7% Beef/Dairy Heifers); 4% Replacement Cattle (27% Bred Cows, 42% Bred Heifers, 27% Cow-Calf Pairs, 3% Heifer Pairs). Feeder cattle over 600 lbs was 55%. Feeder Cattle prices FOB based on net weights after a 0-4% pencil shrink or equivalent, with a 0-40 cent slide > 600 lbs and 0-50 cent slide < 600 lbs.",
